<h1>How to make brownies</h1>
<p><b>ingredients</b></p>
<p>1)Unsalted butter: 1 cup (226g / 2 sticks), melted</p>
<p>2)Granulated sugar: 2 cups (400g) </p>
<p>3)Large eggs: 3 large eggs (room temperature)</p>
<p>4)Vanilla extract: 1 tablespoon  </p>
<p>5)Unsweetened cocoa powder: 3/4 cup </p>
<p>6)All-purpose flour: 1 cup (120g) </p>
<p>7)Salt: 1 teaspoon  </p>
<p>8)Chocolate chips or chunks: 1 1/2 cups  </p>
<p><b>Steps</b></p>
<h2>Ordered List</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Prep the oven and pan: Preheat your oven to 350°F (175°C). Line an 8x8-inch or 9x9-inch metal baking pan with parchment paper.</li>
  
  <li>Melt the butter: Place the butter in a large microwave-safe bowl and heat in short bursts until completely melted.</li>
  <li>Mix the butter, sugar, and cocoa: Stir the cocoa powder and granulated sugar into the warm melted butter. Whisk vigorously so the sugar begins to dissolve and the mixture turns smooth and glossy.</li>
</ol>

